'''Maria Martínez Bayona''' ({{IPA|es|maˈɾia maɾˈtineθ baˈʝona}}; born 1989)<ref name="Meseguer-2026">{{cite web |last=Meseguer |first=Astrid |title=La directora catalana María Martínez Bayona estrenará su ópera prima 'The end of it' en Cannes Première |url=https://www.lavanguardia.com/cultura/20260423/11520922/directora-catalana-maria-martinez-bayona-estrenara-opera-prima-the-end-of-it-cannes-premiere.html |website=[[La Vanguardia]] |access-date=30 April 2026 |language=es |date=23 April 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=García de Francisco |first=Alicia |title=La española Martínez Bayona reflexiona en Cannes sobre la vida eterna en 'The end of it' |url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/la-espa%C3%B1ola-mart%C3%ADnez-bayona-reflexiona-en-cannes-sobre-la-vida-eterna-en-%27the-end-of-it%27/91455861 |website=[[SWI swissinfo]] |access-date=26 May 2026 |language=es |date=21 May 2026}}</ref> is a Spanish director and screenwriter.

==Biography==
Martínez Bayona was born in [[Reus]].<ref name="Meseguer-2026" /><ref>{{cite web |last=Salvà |first=Nando |title=La catalana María Martínez Bayona en Cannes: "Es muy loco que las niñas recurran al 'Retinol' desde los 10 años" |url=https://www.elperiodico.com/es/ocio-y-cultura/20260521/catalana-maria-martinez-bayona-cannes-130515054 |website=[[El Periódico (Barcelona)|El Periódico]] |access-date=26 May 2026 |language=es |date=21 May 2026}}</ref> She studied audiovisual communication at [[Pompeu Fabra University]] before receiving a scholarship from [[La Caixa]] to study at the [[National Film and Television School]] in [[London]] in 2014.<ref>{{cite web |last=Colás |first=Joan |title=Maria Martínez Bayona, la cineasta de Reus que debuta en Cannes con su primera película: "Piqué mucha piedra" |url=https://cronicaglobal.elespanol.com/creacion/20260423/maria-martinez-bayona-cineasta-reus-cannes-pique-mucha-piedra/1003742754763_0.html |website={{ill|Crónica Global|es}} |access-date=30 April 2026 |language=es |date=23 April 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=Beraldi |first=Camila |title=María Martínez Bayona: "Morir da miedo, pero vivir para siempre también" |url=https://www.lavanguardia.com/cultura/20260523/11545787/maria-martinez-bayona-morir-da-miedo-vivir-siempre.html |website=[[La Vanguardia]] |access-date=26 May 2026 |language=es |date=23 May 2026}}</ref>

Her graduation short film, ''Mia'', was long-listed for the [[British Independent Film Award for Best British Short Film]] in 2016.<ref name="Economou-2026">{{cite web |last=Economou |first=Vassilis |title=The End of It to bow in Cannes Première |url=https://cineuropa.org/en/newsdetail/490700 |website=[[Cineuropa]] |access-date=30 April 2026 |date=29 April 2026}}</ref> Her debut feature film, ''[[The End of It]]'', premiered in the Cannes Premiere section of the [[2026 Cannes Film Festival]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Ntim |first=Zac |title='The End Of It:' First Look At Rebecca Hall In Maria Martínez Bayona's Sci-Fi Feature |url=https://deadline.com/2026/02/the-end-of-it-rebecca-hall-maria-martinez-bayona-1236709864/ |website=[[Deadline Hollywood|Deadline]] |access-date=30 April 2026 |date=5 February 2026}}</ref> Her second feature film, ''The First Witch'', will be shot in Catalan, her native language.<ref>{{cite web |last=Hopewell |first=John |title=Fasten Films Revs Up Catalan Cinema (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/global/fasten-films-adria-mones-mar-coll-maria-m-bayona-1236749686/ |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |access-date=26 May 2026 |date=16 May 2026}}</ref>

