'''Adam Sevada''' (born August 8, 1985) is an American [[darts]] player who competes in [[Professional Darts Corporation]] (PDC) and [[World Darts Federation]] (WDF) events. He made his [[PDC World Darts Championship]] debut at the [[2026 PDC World Darts Championship|2026 edition]], where he reached the second round. He also represented the [[United States at the PDC World Cup|United States]] at the [[2026 PDC World Cup of Darts]] alongside teammate [[Stowe Buntz]]. In North America, he has won 11 titles on the Championship Darts Circuit (CDC) Pro Tour and is the reigning [[2026 in PDC#North American Championship|North American champion]].

== Career ==
Before gaining prominence in the [[Professional Darts Corporation]] (PDC) and the Championship Darts Circuit (CDC) in the 2020s, Sevada competed in state and national championships as early as 2008.<ref>{{cite web |date=September 24, 2008 |title=All Native darts team places at state tournament |url=https://www.havasunews.com/parker_pioneer/sports/all-native-darts-team-places-at-state-tournament/article_06d28adf-ecdb-533e-b80c-cf551d470ca7.html |website=Parker Pioneer |access-date=June 29, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=September 16, 2009 |title=Parker resident headed for national darts finals |url=https://www.havasunews.com/parker_pioneer/sports/parker-resident-headed-for-national-darts-finals/article_df0c5202-d549-511c-834e-8eb0088df3eb.html |website=Parker Pioneer |access-date=June 29, 2026}}</ref> He claimed his first CDC title in September 2021, defeating Stephen Phillips 6–4 to win the fourth event of the CDC's [[2021 PDC Pro Tour#USA Tour|2021 USA Tour]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Fraser |first=Brian |date=September 21, 2021 |title=Adam Sevada claims maiden CDC crown |url=https://champdarts.com/main-tour/adam-sevada-claims-maiden-cdc-crown/ |website=Championship Darts Corporation |access-date=June 26, 2026}}</ref>

In 2024, Sevada made his debut in the PDC's [[World Series of Darts]] by qualifying for the [[2024 US Darts Masters]], where he was beaten by [[Rob Cross]] in the first round.<ref>{{cite web |date=June 1, 2024 |title=Littler wins in under 10 minutes on dream US debut |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/darts/articles/c0336gmqjlvo |website=BBC Sport |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref> He won his next two CDC titles during the final weekend of the [[2024 PDC Pro Tour#Championship Darts Circuit (CDC)|2024 CDC Pro Tour]].<ref name="Reaper">{{cite web |last=Fraser |first=Brian |date=September 22, 2024 |title=CDC Judgment Day twice as nice for 'The Reaper' |url=https://champdarts.com/uncategorized/cdc-judgment-day-twice-as-nice-for-the-reaper/ |website=Championship Darts Corporation |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref> The following year, Sevada won a total of five titles on the [[2025 in PDC#Championship Darts Circuit (CDC)|2025 CDC Pro Tour]] to top the rankings and secure a debut at the [[PDC World Darts Championship]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Gorton |first=Josh |date=August 26, 2025 |title=Sevada seals Paddy Power World Darts Championship debut |url=https://www.pdc.tv/news/2025/08/26/sevada-seals-paddy-power-world-darts-championship-debut |website=Professional Darts Corporation |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref> He also took part in the preliminary rounds of the [[2025 PDC World Masters]], finishing second in his group behind [[Karel Sedláček]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Groupstage of PDC World Masters Prelim 2025 |url=https://mastercaller.com/tournaments/world-masters-qualifier/2025/groupstage |website=Mastercaller |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref>

At the [[2026 PDC World Darts Championship|2026 World Championship]], he faced fellow North American competitor [[Matt Campbell (darts player)|Matt Campbell]] in the first round and claimed a 3–1 victory.<ref>{{cite web |last=Davidson |first=Neil |date=December 17, 2025 |title=Canada's Matt (Ginja Ninja) Campbell beaten at world darts championships in London |url=https://www.timescolonist.com/national-sports/canadas-matt-ginja-ninja-campbell-beaten-at-world-darts-championships-in-london-11640039 |website=Times Colonist |access-date=June 29, 2026 |agency=The Canadian Press}}</ref> He was eliminated in a 3–0 defeat to [[Charlie Manby]] in the next round.<ref>{{cite web |last=Chiu |first=Nigel |date=December 23, 2025 |title=World Darts Championship: Luke Humphries thrashes Paul Lim in second round as Gian van Veen, Nathan Aspinall also win |url=https://www.skysports.com/darts/news/12040/13486711/world-darts-championship-luke-humphries-thrashes-paul-lim-in-second-round-as-gian-van-veen-nathan-aspinall-also-win |website=Sky Sports |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref> In June 2026, Sevada partnered [[Stowe Buntz]] to represent the [[United States at the PDC World Cup|United States]] at the [[2026 PDC World Cup of Darts]]. The pair progressed to the second round, where they lost 8–5 to [[Wales at the PDC World Cup|Wales]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Wellens |first=Megan |date=June 13, 2026 |title=World Cup of Darts: England's Luke Littler and Luke Humphries set up clash with Wales in quarters with 8-5 win over Spain |url=https://www.skysports.com/darts/news/12288/13553618/world-cup-of-darts-englands-luke-littler-and-luke-humphries-set-up-clash-with-wales-in-quarters-with-8-5-win-over-spain |website=Sky Sports |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref> Later that month, he won the [[2026 in PDC#North American Championship|North American Championship]] for the first time, defeating [[Jim Long (darts player)|Jim Long]] 6–1 in the final.<ref>{{cite web |last=Gorton |first=Josh |date=June 26, 2026 |title=Superb Sevada storms to bet365 North American Championship title |url=https://www.pdc.tv/news/2026/june/26/superb-sevada-storms-north-american-championship-title/ |website=Professional Darts Corporation |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
Outside of darts, Sevada works at a funeral home in [[Parker, Arizona]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Gutekunst |first=John |date=June 21, 2021 |title=Appreciation dinner held for funeral workers |url=https://www.havasunews.com/parker_pioneer/news/appreciation-dinner-held-for-funeral-workers/article_b44164c0-5425-5fb9-b5bd-44805c80ff33.html |website=Parker Pioneer |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref> He is a member of the [[Colorado River Indian Tribes]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Gutekunst |first=John |date=February 14, 2012 |title=CRIT Juvenile Detention Officers receive certificates |url=https://www.havasunews.com/parker_pioneer/news/crit-juvenile-detention-officers-receive-certificates/article_c55bc2bf-257f-5279-a33f-d6228ae742a3.html |website=Parker Pioneer |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=September 24, 2008 |title=All Native darts team places at state tournament |url=https://www.havasunews.com/parker_pioneer/sports/all-native-darts-team-places-at-state-tournament/article_06d28adf-ecdb-533e-b80c-cf551d470ca7.html |website=Parker Pioneer |access-date=June 27, 2026}}</ref>

